///   allowed size is determined by the size of the cluster's primary node. 25
///   backend server connections are allowed for every 1GB of RAM. Three are
///   reserved for maintenance. For example, a primary node with 1 GB of RAM
///   allows for a maximum of 22 backend server connections while one with 4 GB
///   would allow for 97. Note that these are shared across all connection pools
